# SUBSEQUENT-EVENTS AUDIT FIRST (CLAUDE.md snapshot rule) — 6-K Subsequent Events
# note (R24), which is now the authority and REPLACES the release's prose:
#   IN  — Ulysses (2016-built VLCC): Vessels note (R13) "On May 20, 2026, the
#         Company sold its VLCC tanker Ulysses, for net proceeds of $106,427,
#         realizing a gain of $37,870." Dated BEFORE the snapshot -> proceeds
#         inside Cash; carrying value has LEFT the WC composite; no fleet row.
#         NET proceeds only, no gross price -> NOT promotable to the S&P queue,
#         no back-solve.
#   IN  — Arctic + Antarctic (2007-built Suezmaxes) REPURCHASED: Vessels note
#         (R13) "On May 28, 2026 and June 11, 2026, the Company acquired the two
#         suezmaxes Arctic (Argon Shipping Co.) and Antarctic (Alinda Enterprises
#         Inc.), respectively (Note 4)." BOTH DATES PRECEDE 2026-06-30 -> the pair
#         was OWNED at the snapshot. This REVERSES the 2026-09-11 shadow's
#         conservative OUT (see lease_liabilities and the manifest draft).
#   IN  — Delos T (2026-01-12) + Dion (2026-02-12) MR deliveries, "for an
#         aggregate cost of $95,797" (R13) — already on-curve since Q1.
#   OUT — Anfield DP (DP2 shuttle) delivered 2026-07-28 (R24) -> still a NEWBUILD
#         at 6/30; its instalments sit inside Advances 470,050; joins
#         shuttle_contracted_book at the Q3 refresh.
#   OUT — Archangel sold 2026-08-14; Alaska sold 2026-08-26 (R24). BOTH dated
#         AFTER the snapshot, and the 6/30 balance sheet (R2) carries NO
#         vessels-held-for-sale caption while the Vessels note (R13) carries no
#         held-for-sale sentence -> the pair was OWNED AND NOT HFS at 6/30; rows
#         stay ON-CURVE. This CITES the 2026-09-11 shadow's judgment call (which
#         was taken on the non-conservative side and is now corroborated); the
#         −$2.04/sh flip does not fire.
#   OUT — Series F $0.59375/share paid 2026-07-30; common $1.00/share paid
#         2026-07-30 to holders of record 2026-07-23; Series E $0.57812/share
#         paid 2026-08-28 (R24). The COMMON dividend WAS ACCRUED at the
#         snapshot — see working_capital_net (dividends payable 30,126).
#   No other material subsequent event is disclosed (R24: the Company evaluated
#   subsequent events other than those disclosed through the issuance date).
#
# IMPAIRMENT: Vessels note (R13) "As of June 30, 2026, and December 31, 2025,
# this review did not indicate an impairment charge." No carrying-value haircut.
#
# TEN is the first **3-sleeve hybrid** + first name with `shuttle_contracted_book`
# populated (METHODOLOGY §11.6 off-curve-at-contracted-book convention).

ticker: TEN
quarter: 2026-Q2
