# ::test_sheets_from_2026_q2_carry_ingest_provenance). retrieved_at = the date the
# EDGAR R-renderings of this accession were fetched and this sheet transcribed from
# them. filing_period_end = the interim period end, 2026-06-30.
source_url: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1166663/000119312526394366/d67788d6k.htm
retrieved_at: 2026-09-18
filing_period_end: 2026-06-30

# Cash at 30-Jun-2026: 6-K consolidated balance sheet (R2) "Cash and cash
# equivalents 463,989" + "Restricted cash 2,154" = 466,143 ($K) — the SAME
# construction as the 2026-Q1 sheet's single "Cash" line (321,416) and identical
# to the 2026-09-10 release's "Cash 466,143" (ties to the dollar). Dec-31-2025
# comparative on R2: 293,312 + 4,817 = 298,129, which ties to the audited 20-F.
# Includes the Ulysses net proceeds of 106,427 (R13, sale completed 2026-05-20)
# and is ALREADY NET of the Arctic + Antarctic repurchase consideration
# (2 x 20,000 less 2 x 4,207.5 seller's credit = 31,585 paid; R12) — the manifest
# draft now carries both hulls on-curve, so cash and steel are counted once each.
# The July common dividend of $1.00/share is NOT yet out (paid 2026-07-30) but IS
# accrued at 6/30 inside the WC composite below.
cash_and_equivalents: 466143000

# working_capital_net = Jun-30-2026 COMPOSITE, the SAME construction as the
# 2026-Q1 sheet (Other assets − Other liabilities; Q1: 331,398 − 156,744 =
# 174,654). The 2026-09-11 shadow carried this as "UNVERIFIED at COMPONENT
# level"; the 6-K balance sheet (R2) CLOSES THAT — both composites decompose
# exactly ($K, verified 2026-09-18):
#   Other assets 286,240 = current (total current assets 616,258 − cash and
#     restricted cash 466,143 = 150,115: margin deposits 4,470 + time deposits
#     5,000 + trade receivables net 66,548 + capitalized voyage expenses 1,167 +
#     advances and other 25,652 + inventories 21,702 + debt securities held to
#     maturity ST 15,143 + prepaid insurance and other 3,634 + receivable ST
#     4,418 + current financial instruments FV 2,381)
#     + non-current 136,125 (derivatives 342 + operating-lease RoU 1,700 + other
#     assets 15,233 + debt securities 91,270 + deferred costs 27,580)
#     = 150,115 + 136,125 = 286,240 ✓
#   Other liabilities 220,881 = current (total current liabilities 440,197 −
#     current portion of long-term debt and other financial liabilities 250,376
#     = 189,821: payables 52,876 + due to related companies 9,712 + dividends
#     payable 30,126 + accrued liabilities 82,849 + unearned revenue 11,859 +
#     current operating-lease obligation 1,700 + current financial liability
#     under operating leases 138 + current financial instruments FV 561)
#     + non-current 31,060 (below-market lease net 8,224 + other accrued
#     liabilities 22,726 + derivative liability 110)
#     = 189,821 + 31,060 = 220,881 ✓
#   286,240 − 220,881 = 65,359 ✓ (identical to the release-sourced composite)
# Δ vs Q1 = −109,295, now attributable at component level: the Ulysses
# held-for-sale carrying value has LEFT Other assets (sold 2026-05-20, R13), and
# Other liabilities rose 64,137 on dividends payable 30,126 (2026-07-30 common
# $1.00 x 30,127,603 sh = 30,128 to rounding — the July dividend WAS accrued at
# the snapshot, which the 2026-09-11 shadow flagged as "not disclosed"),
# payables +10,200, accrued liabilities +14,732 and due to related companies
# +6,542 (R2 vs the 20-F Dec-31 comparatives).
# TWO COMPONENTS INSIDE THE COMPOSITE THE OWNER SHOULD SEE (neither changes this
# figure; both are recorded because the composite hid them): (a) dividends
# payable 30,126 — an accrued CLAIM ON COMMON already netted here, so the
# July distribution is not double-counted anywhere; (b) a debt-securities book
# of 106,413 (15,143 short-term held-to-maturity + 91,270 non-current, up from
# 25,233 at Dec-31-2025) sitting INSIDE the composite rather than beside cash —
# a presentation question for the owner, NOT a value question (the figure is in
# NAV either way at the same amount).
# Operating-lease RoU = obligation still nets exactly inside the composite (1,700
# asset vs 1,700 current obligation at 6/30, R2 — Sakura Princess only; see
# lease_liabilities). Tenergy LNG sale-leaseback is a FINANCING arrangement
# (20-F note) — its liability sits in total_debt.
working_capital_net: 65359000

# Total debt at 30-Jun-2026: 6-K consolidated balance sheet (R2) "Current portion
# of long-term debt and other financial liabilities 250,376" + "Long-Term Debt and
# Lease Obligation 1,851,801" = 2,102,177 ($K) — the SAME BS-carrying line the
# 2026-Q1 sheet cites from the Q1 6-K (2,136,109 at Mar-31-2026; Dec-31-2025
# comparative on R2 301,734 + 1,619,241 = 1,920,975, ties to the audited 20-F and
# to the release). BS-carrying convention per the TRMD precedent. Includes the
# Tenergy LNG SL financing arrangement.
# Δ −33,932 in Q2 despite newbuild drawdowns: the Ulysses debt was repaid on the
# 2026-05-20 sale, AND the Arctic + Antarctic finance-lease liability of 39,999
# was DERECOGNIZED on repurchase (R12) — so this figure is already clean of the
# pair's lease obligation while the manifest carries their steel on-curve. No
# double count in either direction.
total_debt: 2102177000

# Lease liabilities = 0 — convention unchanged, and now VERIFIED against the H1-2026
# 6-K (acc 0001193125-26-394366, R12 leases note + R2) rather than
# assumed. At 2026-06-30 the operating-lease population is a SINGLE hull:
#   - Sakura Princess (aframax, SLB 2020-12-21, ASC 842 TRUE SALE, extended one
#     year effective 2025-09-19, incremental borrowing rate 4.55%, remaining term
#     about 0.48 years): 6-K R12 "right-of-use asset of $1,700" at 6/30, and R2
#     shows "Current portion of obligations under operating leases 1,700" — RoU =
#     obligation EXACTLY, netting to zero inside the WC composite above. Not
#     owned; stays out of the manifest.
#   - Arctic + Antarctic have LEFT the lease population. R12: the 2021-06-21
#     five-year sale-and-leaseback (agreed net sale price 52,304 for the pair,
#     seller's credit 8,415) was modified by the 2026-04-07 addendum to
#     repurchase, reclassified as a FINANCE lease, and on repurchase the Company
#     "derecognized the right-of-use assets and the lease liability amounting to
#     $48,362 and $39,999, respectively, and recognized both vessels as fixed
#     assets." The lease liability is therefore NOT in total_debt at 6/30 and NOT
#     here; the two hulls are owned steel on-curve in the manifest draft.
# Tenergy LNG SL is a financing arrangement inside total_debt (20-F note).
lease_liabilities: 0

# Newbuild orderbook at 30-Jun-2026: **TWENTY hulls** under construction —
# 6-K Commitments and Contingencies note (R20): ten DP2 shuttle tankers, two LNG
# carriers, three VLCCs and five LR1s. This RESOLVES the 2026-09-11 shadow's
# open item: the SECOND LNG carrier (release newbuilding-program row 26 "TBN |
# LNG Carrier | Q1 2029", an "Optional Vessel" in the Q1 6-K ex 99.1 table) WAS
# FIRM at or before the snapshot, so the 6/30 orderbook is 20, not the 19 the
# shadow counted. Anfield DP is still inside the 20 at 6/30 (delivered
# 2026-07-28, R24). No per-vessel contract price is disclosed for any hull
# (NEWBUILD_PRICE_PENDING stands on the LNG hull).
#   - Advances paid at Jun-30-2026: 470,050 ($K) — 6-K balance sheet (R2)
#     "Advances for vessels under construction 470,050" (Dec-31-2025 comparative
#     301,868 ties to the audited 20-F; Mar-31-2026 Q1 6-K 442,740). Includes the
#     Anfield DP instalments paid to 6/30.
#   - All NBs treated as **delivered-value = contract-price** (DP2 shuttle per
#     METHODOLOGY §11.6 — no observable resale market; conventional non-shuttle
#     NBs per the conservative read of §3.1) — unchanged from the 2026-Q1 sheet.
#     Net NAV from the NB program = advances paid only.
# Convention: `newbuild_capex_commitments` stays 0 (the remaining future
# obligation will buy delivered vessels of equal value; net NAV impact zero vs
# holding the advances at cost). TEN stays "advances-only" in OFF_CONVENTION_QUEUE
# (tests/test_newbuild_convention.py): no NB rows, no years_to_delivery.
#
# ** OWNER FORK — DO NOT WIRE IN A SHADOW (decisions/ten_shadow_build_2026-09-18.md
# §9.1). ** The remaining commitment is now CITED for the first time. R20: "The
# total contracted amount remaining to be paid for the twenty vessels under
# construction plus the extra costs agreed as of June 30, 2026, was $2,233,409",
# scheduled 228,339 (rest of 2026) / 723,029 (2027) / 1,127,374 (2028) / 154,667
# (2029) — the four legs sum to the total exactly. Against advances of 470,050
# that is about $74/share of gross obligation on 30,127,603 shares which this NAV
# does NOT net. Under §3.1/§9.6 (newbuilds at delivered market LESS remaining
# commitment) this is the TEN instance of the GSL/CMBT/BWLP commitment-net
# convention question. It is a METHODOLOGY decision for the owner, not a sheet
# fix: 0 is kept here because it is the LOCKED convention this sheet has always
# carried, and changing it unilaterally inside a shadow would silently move NAV
# by the largest single leg on the name. Per CLAUDE.md the §9.6 wiring is also
# gated on the name being OUT of NAV_FIGURE_ESTIMATE_QUEUE — which this filing
# now achieves for the commitment figure itself.
newbuild_capex_commitments: 0
newbuild_advances_paid: 470050000

# Diluted common shares outstanding at 30-Jun-2026: 30,127,603 — now ISSUER-STATED
# at the snapshot date, not a 20-F carry. 6-K balance sheet parenthetical (R3):
# common shares $5.00 par, 60,000,000 authorized, 30,805,776 issued, 30,127,603
# outstanding (678,173 treasury) — identical at Dec-31-2025, i.e. NO issuance and
# NO buyback in H1-2026. This CLOSES the 2026-09-11 shadow's UNVERIFIED tag (the
# release printed only the EPS denominator, weighted average 29,972,103, which
# excludes non-vested restricted stock and is not a period-end count).
diluted_shares_outstanding: 30127603

# Preferred equity + NCI (METHODOLOGY §4.2; NCI via preferred_equity — the BWLP
# ratified convention):
#   - Series E: 4,745,947 shares issued (6-K parenthetical R3, $1.00 par,
#                unchanged from Dec-31-2025) x $25.00 redemption = $118,649K
#                9.25% coupon; $0.57812/share paid 2026-08-28 (R24)
#   - Series F: 6,747,147 shares issued (6-K parenthetical R3, $1.00 par,
#                unchanged from Dec-31-2025) x $25.00 redemption = $168,679K
#                9.50% coupon; $0.59375/share paid 2026-07-30 (R24)
#   Total liquidation preference: $287,328K — both series outstanding at 6/30.
# (Tsakos-affiliated entities hold 45,000 Series E + 100,000 Series F per 20-F.)
# PLUS non-controlling interest — 49% of Mare Success S.A. (owns Selini, Salamina,
# Byzantion, Bosporos, all four consolidated at 100% in the fleet manifest) held by
# Polaris Oil Shipping (Flopec affiliate), 20-F Note 11.
#   NCI at 2026-06-30 = **50,130** — taken DIRECTLY from the 6-K balance sheet
#   (R2 "Non-controlling Interest 50,130"; 43,529 at Dec-31-2025). The
#   2026-09-11 shadow ROLLED to this same figure (43,529 + 2,425 Q1 + 4,176 Q2)
#   and tagged the distribution leg UNVERIFIED; the issuer's own balance-sheet
#   figure now CLOSES that — the roll was right, the alternative 45,954 is dead,
#   and no distribution assumption is being made any more.
#   NAV-basis derivation remains not disclosed-derivable (sub-level debt/cash
#   undisclosed) — the standing owner fork at
#   decisions/ten_reconciliation_prereg_2026-07-15.md §6.1, ruled 2026-07-15 in
#   favour of the booked figure.
#   287,328 + 50,130 = 337,458 (2026-Q1 sheet: 287,328 + 45,954 = 333,282)
preferred_equity: 337458000

# Governance / structural-NAV-trap discount (METHODOLOGY §15, NEW 2026-06-06):
# TEN is the framework's first §15 case — a controlled FPI structure where
# the market consistently applies a 50-60% P/NAV discount. Drivers per
# external read + user analysis:
#   - Controlled-shareholder structure (Tsakos family); related-party
#     transactions including management fees to Tsakos Columbia Shipmanagement
#   - Low common payout: $1.50/share against ~$8 EPS in 2026 (~19% payout
#     ratio); 36% YoY increase is "highest dividend in 10 years" but still
#     well below mainstream tanker-cycle peers (DHT/NAT 100%, FRO 80%)
#   - No buyback program; retained capital deployed into a $2.4B NB orderbook
#     whose returns to common are uncertain
#   - Preferred E+F structure ($287M aggregate) with Tsakos-affiliated owners
#     holding meaningful slugs (0.95% E + 1.5% F per 20-F)
#
# 30% NAV haircut chosen to bring tool PW FV into the neighborhood of VIE
# Bullish $51.50 — i.e., interpret VIE's already-discounted target as the
# anchor for what the market will pay rather than what the assets are worth.
# Conservative read: even VIE Bullish applies ~47% discount vs unconstrained
# NAV; our 30% sits in between full-realisation (0%) and VIE Bullish (47%),
# allowing room for partial governance improvement vs full continuation of
# the historical discount. Judgmental; revisit when governance signals shift
# (e.g., capital-return policy change, management transition, M&A).
#
# Applied at the BLEND layer (NAV term) and on the strip's TERMINAL value —
# both are NAV-realisation computations. Interim DPS are NOT haircut (already-
# realised cash to common). Broker-NAV sweep operates on undiscounted NAV
# (the question "what are the assets worth" is independent of "what will
# common shareholders capture").
#
# SHADOW 2026-09-18 — HOLD 0.30, BUT THE DRIVER IS NOW QUANTIFIED FOR THE FIRST
# TIME AND THIS IS AN OWNER CALL (record §9.2). The 2026-09-11 shadow noted "the
# release carries no related-party fee figure"; the 6-K related-party note (R34)
# supplies them for H1-2026 ($K): Tsakos Energy Management fees 14,659 (H1-2025:
# 10,217, +43.5%) of which supervisory services 2,171; INCENTIVE AWARDS 5,000
# (H1-2025: 3,000, +66.7%); Tsakos Shipping and Trading chartering commission
# 6,602 at a stated 1.25% rate, technical services 1,034, delivery commission
# 250; Argosy Insurance 9,036; AirMania Travel 3,432 — about 40,013 of H1
# related-party outflow, roughly $80M annualised against H1 net income of
# $228.1M. The same 6-K note R34 (period ended 2026-06-30) also discloses
# contracted FUTURE MANAGEMENT FEES PAYABLE, as the issuer estimates them, of
# 13,843 (2026) / 27,702 (2027) / 29,136 (2028) / 30,114 (2029) / 30,108 (2030)
# / 119,521 (2031-2035) = about 250,424 contracted to the manager.
# The §15.7 working band is 30-36%. This evidence points to the UPPER half, but
# the haircut is JUDGMENTAL and a shadow does not move a judgmental NAV lever —
# 0.30 is held unchanged so the owner rules on a clean comparison. Sensitivity is
# in the record (§9.2). Revisit with the November 2026 dividend announcement.
governance_discount_pct: 0.30

# Shuttle contracted-book (METHODOLOGY §11.6, NEW 2026-06-05 PM): NPV of the 4
# in-water DP2 shuttle tankers at contracted day rates + Suezmax-curve residual
# at TC expiry, discounted at WACC 11%, utilization 98.3%, offhire 1%, daily opex
# $11,000/day (~10% premium over conventional Suezmax) — carried UNCHANGED from
# the 2026-Q1 sheet. Anfield DP (delivered 2026-07-28, R24) is OUT of the 6/30
# snapshot and joins this book at the Q3 refresh.
#
# Per-vessel breakdown (npv = revenue NPV − opex NPV + residual NPV @ TC expiry):
#   Brasil 2014   $104.8M  ($58,908/d → $60k extension; ext to 2033-11; age 20.5; residual $14.7M NPV)
#   Rio 2016      $104.2M  ($58,403/d → $60k extension; ext to 2033-10; age 20.6; residual $14.6M NPV)
#   Athens 04     $121.5M  ($58,569/d through 2032-05; age 7.0; residual $45.4M NPV; high residual)
#   Paris 24      $122.6M  ($58,569/d through 2032-08; age 6.9; residual $44.4M NPV; high residual)
#   --
#   TOTAL         $453.1M
#
# UNVERIFIED (shadow): awaits a Brasil/Rio EXTENSION-RATE disclosure and a
# re-strike as-of 2026-06-30. **This is the ONE remaining uncited NAV-moving
# figure on the sheet and it is the reason this shadow reads WOULD-HOLD.** The
# H1-2026 6-K carries NO per-vessel shuttle day rates (no fleet or employment
# table of any kind), so:
#   (a) the $60,000/day extension rate for Brasil 2014 / Rio 2016 remains an
#       APPROX of the "increased rate" disclosed in the Q1 6-K subsequent events
#       (2026-04-23) — a `~`-grade input on a $453.1M NAV leg (about 16% of gross
#       NAV), and per CLAIM/FIGURE provenance an APPROX is a RED, not data;
#   (b) the NPV is struck as-of 2026-03-31 and is NOT re-struck at 6/30: the ages
#       inside the breakdown are the Q1 build's, and one quarter of contracted
#       margin (4 hulls x 91 days x ($58.5k rate less $11k opex) x 0.983
#       utilisation, about $17M) has been collected into Cash 466,143 while still
#       counted inside this NPV; net of the 11% unwind (about $12M) the overlap is
#       about $5M (about $0.15/sh), NON-CONSERVATIVE.
# Re-strike at the live land (the Q3 refresh also adds Anfield DP). The resolution
# path is the monthly data kit (per-vessel TC rates), not the 6-K.
shuttle_contracted_book: 453100000

# held_for_sale: key deliberately ABSENT (loader default 0), as in the 2026-Q1
# sheet (decisions/ten_reconciliation_prereg_2026-07-15.md §2 ruled "0
# (deliberate)"). Now CITED rather than assumed: the 6/30 balance sheet (R2)
# carries NO vessels-held-for-sale caption and the Vessels note (R13) carries no
# held-for-sale sentence; Ulysses was SOLD 2026-05-20 (not HFS at 6/30) and
# Archangel / Alaska were sold 2026-08-14 / 2026-08-26, both AFTER the snapshot
# (R24), so both remain owned, operating and on-curve at 6/30.
